course: dictionary
lesson: 15295
title: Words with a body inside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words hide a clue in their root. Skeletal comes from skeleton, the frame of bones inside a body, and the ending -al means to do with. So skeletal means to do with that frame: «The skeletal system holds up the body.»
explain: Skeletal can also describe someone or something very thin, with the bones showing. «The skeletal horse could barely stand.» A horse is not a skeleton, but the sentence tells you it looks like one. Ask: what would a starved, very thin horse look like? That is the meaning.
explain: Skeletal can mean only the most basic parts, with little else. «The team was a skeletal crew of just three people.» Three people is not a full team, so skeletal means stripped down to the bare minimum. Test it: does "a bare minimum crew of three" fit? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Skeletal means to do with the skeleton, the frame of bones inside a body.
fact: An adult human has 206 bones in the skeletal system.
fact: «Skeletal» can mean very thin, so that the bones show.
fact: «Skeletal» can mean only the most basic parts, as in «a skeletal plan».
fact: Skeletal muscles are the ones we control, like the muscles in our arms and legs.
exercise: «The skeletal system supports the body and protects the brain and heart.» What is the skeletal system? | The food in the stomach | The skin and hair that cover the body | *The frame of bones inside the body | The blood moving round the body
exercise: «The old film showed a skeletal figure in the dark.» What does skeletal suggest here? | Soft and fluffy | Very large and strong | *Spooky, thin and like a bare bone frame | Bright and colourful
exercise: «The doctor was worried, because the patient looked skeletal.» What does skeletal suggest? | Tall and strong | *Very thin, with the bones showing | Happy and well fed | Full of energy and ready to run
test: «After the storm, the shop had a skeletal staff of only four workers.» What does skeletal mean here? | Brand new and shiny | Made of bone | *Reduced to the most basic number needed | Very large and busy
test: Why might a skeletal look worry a doctor? | It shows the patient is on holiday | It means the patient has too many bones | *It can be a sign of illness or hunger | It means the patient is very strong
exam: Which sentence uses skeletal to mean the frame of bones inside a body? | «The skeletal crew cheered when the match was won.» | «The skeletal fog covered the hills in the morning.» | *«The skeletal system protects the heart and lungs.» | «The skeletal plan was short and simple.»
